## What is a code block?

## The syntax

This is an inline code block, `console.log('hello world')`.

This is a code block.

{% fence
   content="import { getCollection } from \"astro:content\";\n\nexport async function getAllPosts() {\n\tconst res = await getCollection(\"posts\", ({ data }) => {\n\t\treturn import.meta.env.PROD ? data.draft !== true : true;\n\t});\n\n\tif (!res) {\n\t\tthrow Error(\"[api/v1/posts]: Internal Server Error\");\n\t}\n\n\tconst posts = res.sort((a, b) => b.data.createdAt.valueOf() - a.data.createdAt.valueOf());\n\n\treturn posts;\n}"
   language="ts"
   title="Posts.ts"
   frame="auto" /%}

